<h2>The statutory lock, in three provisions</h2>
<div class="tiles">
  <div class="tile"><strong>Order 23 Rule 3.</strong> The gateway: a lawful agreement in writing and signed by the parties, proved to the court&rsquo;s satisfaction, is recorded and decreed. The proviso channels every dispute about whether such a compromise occurred back to the same court.</div>
  <div class="tile"><strong>Rule 3A.</strong> The closed door: no suit lies to set aside a decree on the ground that the compromise was not lawful — the challenge cannot migrate to a new case before a new judge.</div>
  <div class="tile"><strong>Section 96(3).</strong> The sealed window: no appeal from a decree passed with the parties&rsquo; consent, reflecting estoppel by consent and the policy of ending settled litigation.</div>
